# Specs — TRACKED. A spec is the durable design record for a feature, so it must
# survive outside the worktree that produced it (another machine, CI, a reviewer).
# Only the transient run-state written *inside* a spec directory stays ignored:
#   - progress.md: loop's own words are "deleted on clean EXIT, never auto-committed,
#     safe to .gitignore" (skills/loop/SKILL.md:439)
#   - dot-prefixed .tmp files: decompose's atomic-rename staging
#     (skills/decompose/SKILL.md:181, 350)
specs/**/progress.md
specs/**/.*.tmp

# Local workspace / agent working files (incl. timestamped backups)
_workspace*/

# pilot-verify run artifact — coherence-audit writes its report beside the specs it audits
skills/coherence-audit/scripts/tests/portability-fixture/coherence-report.md
